  "id": "cognitive-intelligence",
  "term": "cognitive intelligence",
  "definition": "In this historical source, cognitive intelligence means the distinctly human capacity to go beyond simple recognition of objects and to think in abstractions. It includes forming concepts of a class or type by comparing experiences, grouping shared qualities, and setting aside differences rather than relying only on concrete mental images.",
